Fulltext search ngram parser plugin to support
CONTAINS queries via InnoDB fulltext indexes.

# Usage

Ensure minimum token size configuration:

```
-- Configure ngram token size with ngram_token_size,
-- and set innodb_ft_min_token_size for InnoDB fulltext search to at least the
-- same value.
SET GLOBAL ngram_token_size = 3;
SET GLOBAL innodb_ft_min_token_size = 3;

-- Enable diagnostic print for debugging if needed
SET GLOBAL innodb_ft_enable_diag_print = 1;

-- Alternatively, you can set these in the configuration file or CLI flags
--ngram_token_size=3 --innodb_ft_min_token_size=3 --innodb-ft-enable-diag-print=1
```

Check plugin is loaded:

```sql
SHOW PLUGINS SONAME 'ngram.so';

or

SHOW PLUGINS LIKE 'ngram';
```

Load the plugin if not loaded:

```sql
INSTALL PLUGIN ngram SONAME 'ngram.so';
```

Create a fulltext index with the ngram parser:

```sql
CREATE TABLE my_table (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    content TEXT,
    FULLTEXT(content) WITH PARSER ngram
) ENGINE=InnoDB;

-- Pay attention to the engine as the default one may be not InnoDB, and it may
-- not support FTS.

INSERT INTO my_table (content) VALUES
('This is a sample text for fulltext search.'),
('Another example of text to search.');
```
Use it in a query:

```sql
SELECT * FROM my_table WHERE MATCH(content) AGAINST('amp');

+----+--------------------------------------------+
| id | content                                    |
+----+--------------------------------------------+
| 1  | This is a sample text for fulltext search. |
| 2  | Another example of text to search.         |
+----+--------------------------------------------+
```
